# rig's systemd --user unit (PLAN.md section 5l).
#
# THIS UNIT DELIBERATELY HAS NO ExecStop, AND THE ABSENCE IS LOAD-BEARING.
# Do not add one. cmd/rigd/unit_test.go fails if anybody does, because a rule
# whose only enforcement is a comment is the thing this repo keeps paying for.
#
# THE SCAR, and it was paid for on this machine rather than read about.
# AgentBox's unit carried ExecStop=agentbox quit. agentbox is single-instance
# by flock and auto-spawns on first use, so `agentbox daemon` prints "already
# running" and exits 0 when one is up. systemd sees a Type=simple main process
# exit successfully, decides the service finished, and runs ExecStop - which
# killed the healthy daemon that was already serving. Enabling the unit left
# the desktop with no agentbox at all.
#
# rig has the identical shape: section 5f is a single-instance flock, section
# 5g auto-spawns on the first client call, and section 18's SIGTERM path is
# the same graceful drain a stop command would use. So the unit needs no stop
# verb, and adding one recreates a defect already paid for once here. This
# holds for `rig down` too: the lesson is not "no signal to a pid", it is no
# stop command in any form. `agentbox quit` was not a signal either.
#
# IT MANAGES production ONLY, and by construction rather than by a flag
# somebody might omit (section 37, precondition 5). It sets no
# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR and passes no --estate, so it inherits the ordinary
# environment and reaches the default runtime directory, which is
# production's. development is always placed explicitly, so this unit cannot
# reach it.
#
# ONE WRINKLE, INHERITED AND ACCEPTED: start the unit while a daemon is
# already up and the unit reports inactive while that daemon keeps serving.
# At login - the case this unit exists for - nothing is running yet, so it
# starts one and stays active.

[Unit]
Description=rig, the estate platform
Documentation=https://github.com/boris-milner/rig

# graphical-session.target, not default.target: rig needs the session bus and
# the display for section 12's toasts and section 11's tray.
PartOf=graphical-session.target
After=graphical-session.target

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/rigd
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=2

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical-session.target
